{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes","id":1507350,"title":"Order of the Bitter Ashes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-04-03T19:04:53-07:00","id":1507350,"title":"Order of the Bitter Ashes","content":"Have you ever used/seen the Grail/Ashen Knights in your chronicles? If so, how did that go?<br /> What's your overall opinion on them in the Dark Ages setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T19:19:49-07:00","id":1507353,"title":"","content":"I've played one, I enjoyed the experience and thematics as far as the Grail Knight vibe. There's a certain built in angst level in knowing where they end up, but no more so than when you're playing a Salubri really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T19:30:54-07:00","id":1507354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes?p=1507353#post1507353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've played one, I enjoyed the experience and thematics as far as the Grail Knight vibe. There's a certain built in angst level in knowing where they end up, but no more so than when you're playing a Salubri really.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like their theme as well. I think the Grail gives us many possibilities as even the Order's Scholars aren't really sure if it's really the True Holy Grail. The effects of the Grail embrace are also fascinating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T19:48:12-07:00","id":1507357,"title":"","content":"The whole &quot;is this whole experiment in fact a mistake&quot; aspect is interesting as well, yeah. The &quot;when we try to have humans drink from it they die&quot; adds a certain touch of perhaps the Gatherers mis-stepped. I suppose I enjoy that it adds a bit of a sense of, perhaps the Grail Knights shouldn't have been in the first place, but all the same they tried to do what good they could in the time they had before the age and their own standards consumed them. It's tragic in the ways that I enjoy as far as that sort of tragedy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-03T20:11:07-07:00","id":1507359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes?p=1507357#post1507357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The whole &quot;is this whole experiment in fact a mistake&quot; aspect is interesting as well, yeah. The &quot;when we try to have humans drink from it they die&quot; adds a certain touch of perhaps the Gatherers mis-stepped. I suppose I enjoy that it adds a bit of a sense of, perhaps the Grail Knights shouldn't have been in the first place, but all the same they tried to do what good they could in the time they had before the age and their own standards consumed them. It's tragic in the ways that I enjoy as far as that sort of tragedy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! It's really bizarre that the Grail Embrace doesn't work on humans. The whole set of possibilities that exist regarding the true nature of the Grail, the doubts surrounding it and when you take into account that for the mentality of the time, there was no such a thing as skepticism as nowadays. So they act doing what they believe is good and true, with faith, etc. But there's always that shroud of doubt.<br /> <br /> To be honest, I think they differ from the Salubri, because the way I see it, the Salubri always have &quot;some shades of gray&quot;, in the sense that they could be just crazy lunatics or soul stealers as the Tremere call them, and when you take into account the doubts surrounding Saulot's true purpose and his history, etc., it adds another dimension to them.<br /> I don't understand people who disregard the Salubri as &quot;anti-theme&quot; in a vampire game, I think it's quite the opposite, they have a lot of potential in not really being the &quot;good guys&quot; or being in service of a &quot;megalomaniac Machiavellian monster&quot; or even the victims of his madness (I mean if one takes into consideration that perhaps he found in the Tremere better instruments to achieve his purposes and basically discarded the Salubri after &quot;their faillure&quot;, etc.).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-04T10:57:19-07:00","id":1507419,"title":"","content":"I loved the idea of the order, but I'd never played one myself and maybe one day a good idea will come to me to use them in a story. I do like the setting of the Dark Ages in general and have tried to play it once or twice. But my heart is more in the Victorian and Wild West settings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 04-04-2023, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T00:45:13-07:00","id":1507459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes?p=1507419#post1507419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I loved the idea of the order, but I'd never played one myself and maybe one day a good idea will come to me to use them in a story. I do like the setting of the Dark Ages in general and have tried to play it once or twice. But my heart is more in the Victorian and Wild West settings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm a fan of Dark Ages since I started playing and decided to be a ST more than 2 decades ago. My very first time I played vampire was in a Dark Ages setting and I remember that I played Vampire Redemption at the time, I've always been a fan of the scenario. I think it's much &quot;darker&quot; (duh lol, sorry) than modern setting with all its technologies and &quot;easiness of life&quot;. Too much light for my taste.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T04:29:26-07:00","id":1507470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes#post1507350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's your overall opinion on them in the Dark Ages setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is really nice, good, curious, and interesting to read about Vampires who are knights ( or monks, or esteemed aristocrats and ladies ) featured prominently in VtM's Dark Ages books.<br /> This really does remind me of for example VtM: Redemption ; and also of my initial exploration and understanding of the World of Darkness as an RPG game and as a setting.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T08:05:18-07:00","id":1507482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes#post1507350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you ever used/seen the Grail/Ashen Knights in your chronicles? If so, how did that go?<br /> What's your overall opinion on them in the Dark Ages setting?</div> </div> </div> </div>I<br /> <br /> I give my opinion here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/podcast/the-ashen-knight\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/5f352e879e84e0597aeaee4d/t/60ba44db93e1ff23640fb002/1622820066568/51PPHCPTZQL.jpg?format=1500w\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/podcast/the-ashen-knight\" target=\"_blank\"> The Ashen Knight </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/podcast/the-ashen-knight\" target=\"_blank\"> https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/podcast/the-ashen-knight </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A look at knights, knighthood, and chivalry in the Dark Medieval. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance Writer and Storyteller's Vault contributor. Find my work here: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/index.php?affiliate_id=17903\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.storytellersvault.com/ind...liate_id=17903</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1535-jackob","name":"Jackob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1535_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T09:32:29-07:00","id":1507487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes?p=1507459#post1507459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'm a fan of Dark Ages since I started playing and decided to be a ST more than 2 decades ago. My very first time I played vampire was in a Dark Ages setting and I remember that I played Vampire Redemption at the time, I've always been a fan of the scenario. I think it's much &quot;darker&quot; (duh lol, sorry) than modern setting with all its technologies and &quot;easiness of life&quot;. Too much light for my taste.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough on that point. But a point could be made that the stakes are higher with the advancement of technologies that make there existence harder and how a slip up can have even more deadly consquences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T14:28:03-07:00","id":1507515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jackob</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes?p=1507482#post1507482\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I<br /> <br /> I give my opinion here:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/podcast/the-ashen-knight\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"http://static1.squarespace.com/static/5f352e879e84e0597aeaee4d/t/60ba44db93e1ff23640fb002/1622820066568/51PPHCPTZQL.jpg?format=1500w\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/podcast/the-ashen-knight\" target=\"_blank\"> The Ashen Knight </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/podcast/the-ashen-knight\" target=\"_blank\"> https://wodarkages.squarespace.com/podcast/the-ashen-knight </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> A look at knights, knighthood, and chivalry in the Dark Medieval. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh very good! I'm surely going to listen to your thoughts about it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T14:40:29-07:00","id":1507517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes?p=1507470#post1507470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It is really nice, good, curious, and interesting to read about Vampires who are knights ( or monks, or esteemed aristocrats and ladies ) featured prominently in VtM's Dark Ages books.<br /> This really does remind me of for example VtM: Redemption ; and also of my initial exploration and understanding of the World of Darkness as an RPG game and as a setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes! I have fond memories of VtM: Redemption. I think there's &quot;a magic&quot; in the mystery of the Dark Ages setting and its many possibilities. It's a pity that it seems it unfortunately did not make the same success of the modern setting. More than 90% of my games during all these years of storytelling(more than 20) were set in the Dark Ages, some of them reached the modern times, most did not. I'm a real fan of chronicles that stretches for centuries. Most of mine follow this pattern.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12348,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","user":"Herr Meister","date":". 04-06-2023, 01:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T18:59:02-07:00","id":1507527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes?p=1507517#post1507517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes! I have fond memories of VtM: Redemption. I think there's &quot;a magic&quot; in the mystery of the Dark Ages setting and its many possibilities. It's a pity that it seems it unfortunately did not make the same success of the modern setting. More than 90% of my games during all these years were set in the Dark Ages, some of them reached the modern times, most did not. I'm a real fan of chronicles stretches for centuries. Most of mine follow this pattern.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just to very quickly counter a thing before the idea takes on a life of its own for being spoken aloud, the Dark Ages setting was plenty successful, especially the Vampire part of it. It had three editions and a whole bunch of books across several years. Most games are lucky to get a fraction of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T22:54:57-07:00","id":1507553,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes?p=1507527#post1507527\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just to very quickly counter a thing before the idea takes on a life of its own for being spoken aloud, the Dark Ages setting was plenty successful, especially the Vampire part of it. It had three editions and a whole bunch of books across several years. Most games are lucky to get a fraction of that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It's great to know that, I often thought it wasn't the case because you see V5 basically discarded it, so I thought it was because it wasn't as successful as the other settings. Thanks for clarifying that to me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T23:18:26-07:00","id":1507556,"title":"","content":"I've ran the game Under the Black Cross (which covers somewhat badly the confront between the invader Jurgen and the Tectonics, against Vladimir Rustovitch and the voivodes). In it, during the second chapter (which is a great chapter for any chroncile), which occurs in Acre, there is the appearance of a member from the Bitter Ashes, and he can be a big help.<br /> I find it interesting that he feels different than any other faction in the city, cuz he just wants the artifact for the sake of it. He doesn't care for who he must pay heed or help, but he won't work for anyone either, still being a knight in service to his order only.<br /> <br /> It was studying more about the order that I found how these gray knights are truly strange. Their skin is more grayish and mineral-looking if I'm not recalling wrong. They also resist fire, sun and faith much more because of their effect of the Grail. So they might stride towards holy relics with lesser hardship than most Kindred, which is cool.<br /> <br /> The Dark Age era had such an awesome amount of lore, but very little was actually used or set for use. Much was just stated to exist or alluded. The order of bitter ashes is an example of that. Besides that, when there are chronicles like Under Black Cross, and Transylvania Chronicles, they are disjointed, stern and unmalleable. This will happen like that, and the best you can do is roll a bit better to not suffer as much damage, which is lame and irritating. The second chapter of UtBC, in Acre, is actually a great one, leaving PCs to investigate as they desire, politic, explore, and in the end sway the destiny of the city to where they desire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-05T23:51:58-07:00","id":1507558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've ran the game Under the Black Cross (which covers somewhat badly the confront between the invader Jurgen and the Tectonics, against Vladimir Rustovitch and the voivodes). In it, during the second chapter (which is a great chapter for any chroncile), which occurs in Acre, there is the appearance of a member from the Bitter Ashes, and he can be a big help.<br /> I find it interesting that he feels different than any other faction in the city, cuz he just wants the artifact for the sake of it. He doesn't care for who he must pay heed or help, but he won't work for anyone either, still being a knight in service to his order only.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>I've run Under the Black Cross as well, but it evolved into an entire chronicle from that point and it kind of went away from the central theme of the beginning. I quite like J\u00fcrgen, by the way, I really enjoyed his role in the Dark Ages Ventrue Nove, as a sidenote I REALLY loved all Dark Ages Novels. You actually made me want to reread the second chapter of Under the Black Cross. The setting could've been explored much more than it was in my opinion. There's so much potential in it, that it's a pity it was somewhat wasted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T02:33:58-07:00","id":1507565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes?p=1507517#post1507517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes! I have fond memories of VtM: Redemption. </div> </div> </div> </div>It was one of the many games I clearly and definitely noticed when I was a teenager. There was a detailed review, and also a precise guide, with images and pictures, in a Polish computer games periodical.<br /> <br /> Back then when I was younger it was that I was distinctly more interested in game series like Warcraft, Heroes of Might and Magic, Total War, and also of course Age of Empires. <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes?p=1507517#post1507517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think there's &quot;a magic&quot; in the mystery of the Dark Ages setting and its many possibilities. It's a pity that it seems it unfortunately did not make the same success of the modern setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>No matter how many books and paragraphs Vampire Dark Ages has, it is definitely a major and important part of the World of Darkness. In fact simillar could definitely be said in regard to every WoD game line They each have their own mood, atmosphere, art style, purpose, story approach, mood, theme, concepts, mechanics, and ideas.<br /> <br /> I especially like the more specialized and focused books, like the <i>Ashen Thief </i>, and <i>Lord Liege Lackey </i>, and <i>Three Pillars </i>, and<i> Player's Guide to Low Clans </i>, and<i> Player's Guide to High Clans,</i> and<i> Dark Ages: British Isles</i> , and<i> Road of Kings </i>, and<i> Road of Heaven </i>, and<i> Road of Sin</i>.<br /> <br /> The <i>Three Pillars</i> supplement is distinctly worth reading for it's clear themes and interesting variety.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T03:34:29-07:00","id":1507571,"title":"","content":"<i>Under the Black Cross</i> is a distinctly odd book in that the writers clearly wanted to write a novel, and, as a result, end up creating a book with lots of what might best be described as &quot;quirks&quot;. The first story is effectively a mystery in which there is only one suspect, the second story is clearly shoe-horned into the rest of the chronicle, whilst the third story seems to give up on any notion of player agency or, indeed, the established notion of how Cainites behave in the setting. <br /> <br /> From the above, the observant reader may guess that I'm not a fan of the book...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T13:13:13-07:00","id":1507598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes?p=1507553#post1507553\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It's great to know that, I often thought it wasn't the case because you see V5 basically discarded it, so I thought it was because it wasn't as successful as the other settings. Thanks for clarifying that to me!</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than a one off reference to the line in one of its earlier books, V5 discarded it, I imagine, because thematically V5 is not interested in such things as Dark Ages focused on, being that V5 is a game about &quot;right immediately now&quot; as hard as it can possibly be. It's a game whose official wiki at this point takes the stance of that anything that does not directly appear in a V5 book should not be considered game content.<br /> <br /> Whether you like that or not (and I don't personally, but some people do, so), it is at this point a game with a trajectory that is increasingly uninterested in what existed before it, and that includes the DA line. The idea that said line wasn't successful wouldn't be borne out by the simple logic of having had a multi edition product line. Vampire: the Dark Ages, Dark Ages Vampire, and DAV20th, and the various supplements for all of those all existed and did fine for themselves for what they were.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T13:46:53-07:00","id":1507600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MarkK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes?p=1507598#post1507598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Other than a one off reference to the line in one of its earlier books, V5 discarded it, I imagine, because thematically V5 is not interested in such things as Dark Ages focused on, being that V5 is a game about &quot;right immediately now&quot; as hard as it can possibly be. It's a game whose official wiki at this point takes the stance of that anything that does not directly appear in a V5 book should not be considered game content.<br /> <br /> Whether you like that or not (and I don't personally, but some people do, so), it is at this point a game with a trajectory that is increasingly uninterested in what existed before it, and that includes the DA line. The idea that said line wasn't successful wouldn't be borne out by the simple logic of having had a multi edition product line. Vampire: the Dark Ages, Dark Ages Vampire, and DAV20th, and the various supplements for all of those all existed and did fine for themselves for what they were.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I couldn't be more disappointed than I was with V5. For all intents and purposes it threw away everything that was so great about the WoD in what seems to be, in my opinion, another gamble. I remember that I was upset when they did something not so different when they decided to end the WoD with Gehenna books, etc, and decided to start anew with Requiem. At the time I said, &quot;they'll certainly regret it and move back to the previous setting, because it's too good to be abandoned like that&quot;. When V20 came, I thought that my old prevision was right, but then yet another gamble is being made with V5. I enjoyed many of the powers and system for these said powers in V5 and I adapt many of them to my V20 table (that's been running for more than 10 years, before DAV20 we were playing Dark Ages Vampire with a lot of Homebrew and adapted to V20 which wasn't much different from the earlier edition).<br /> <br /> I could say that they're going to move back to the radical changes they made, but at this point I'm not so sure and honestly don't really care that much anymore, my group and I play with a lot of houserules and use the amazing set the Dark Ages line provide us. If V5 decides to change its direction and publish a Dark Ages supplement, I'm surely going to take a look at, but other than that I'm quite content in not paying much attention to the &quot;new setting&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T13:50:15-07:00","id":1507601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Back then when I was younger it was that I was distinctly more interested in game series like Warcraft, Heroes of Might and Magic, Total War, and also of course Age of Empires.<br /> \u200b </div> </div> </div>Just as I sidenote, I remember those days, I was once a professional Warcraft 3, The Frozen Throne player, by the way. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No matter how many books and paragraphs Vampire Dark Ages has, it is definitely a major and important part of the World of Darkness. In fact simillar could definitely be said in regard to every WoD game line They each have their own mood, atmosphere, art style, purpose, story approach, mood, theme, concepts, mechanics, and ideas. </div> </div> </div>I totally agree here, and I'll say it again that I love the unique mood and atmosphere of the Dark Ages setting. I'm perhaps just as fascinated as I was as a kid back then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T14:18:18-07:00","id":1507604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes?p=1507600#post1507600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be honest, I couldn't be more disappointed than I was with V5. For all intents and purposes it threw away everything that was so great about the WoD in what seems to be, in my opinion, another gamble. I remember that I was upset when they did something not so different when they decided to end the WoD with Gehenna books, etc, and decided to start anew with Requiem. At the time I said, &quot;they'll certainly regret it and move back to the previous setting, because it's too good to be abandoned like that&quot;. When V20 came, I thought that my old prevision was right, but then yet another gamble is being made with V5. I enjoyed many of the powers and system for these said powers in V5 and I adapt many of them to my V20 table (that's been running for more than 10 years, before DAV20 we were playing Dark Ages Vampire with a lot of Homebrew and adapted to V20 which wasn't much different from the earlier edition).<br /> <br /> I could say that they're going to move back to the radical changes they made, but at this point I'm not so sure and honestly don't really care that much anymore, my group and I play with a lot of houserules and use the amazing set the Dark Ages line provide us. If V5 decides to change its direction and publish a Dark Ages supplement, I'm surely going to take a look at, but other than that I'm quite content in not paying much attention to the &quot;new setting&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>While somewhat ironically for a game laser focused on the immediate now, Vampire 5th has existed as its own gameline for five years at this point, they're not going to move back from that, no, and I wouldn't expect them to. The recent player's guide is if anything a doubling down on that commitment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12141-markk","name":"MarkK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"493"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T15:14:41-07:00","id":1507609,"title":"","content":"My only real problem with the setting is that you knew what was going to happen to some of these characters or kingdoms according to the VTM. I.E. if you liked the character De Ruiz as your character's sire. You had to have it before 1424 when his childe Moncada would overthrow him as the dominant member of the Lasombra clan in Spain.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-06T16:00:26-07:00","id":1507617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes?p=1507609#post1507609\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only real problem with the setting is that you knew what was going to happen to some of these characters or kingdoms according to the VTM. I.E. if you liked the character De Ruiz as your character's sire. You had to have it before 1424 when his childe Moncada would overthrow him as the dominant member of the Lasombra clan in Spain.</div> </div> </div> </div>But then the interesting thing in Dark Ages game, in my opinion at least, is that we can change history. I never let those events set in stone and adapt to whatever happen in the story I'm running (btw, unsurprisingly, players love to change history lol).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T12:30:53-07:00","id":1508173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herr Meister</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes?p=1507617#post1507617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But then the interesting thing in Dark Ages game, in my opinion at least, is that we can change history. I never let those events set in stone and adapt to whatever happen in the story I'm running (btw, unsurprisingly, players love to change history lol).</div> </div> </div> </div>True I do know that many of the posters here have taken big creative liberties with the ongoing metaplot. We got rid of the Sabbat in ours and now it's a cold war with the Anarchs and Camarilla power blocs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-12T20:03:04-07:00","id":1508234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1507350-order-of-the-bitter-ashes?p=1508173#post1508173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> 